<title>FRANCE: Ivory Coast minister denies cocoa stores full.</title>
<headline>Ivory Coast minister denies cocoa stores full.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ivory Coast's agriculture minister denied on Wednesday industry reports that cocoa warehouses at the country's ports are at or near full capacity.</p>
<p>&quot;There is considerable fluidity at our ports,&quot; Lambert Kouassi Konan told Reuters in Paris where he was attending a farm show.</p>
<p>Industry sources in Abidjan have said that warehouses at Ivory Coast ports are full to a capacity of around 400,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Kouassi did not give a figure for the amount in storage but said that the reports of full warehouses were not true.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
